    Document    : healthTracker.xml
    Description : Backing flowsheet for the CARLOS Health Tracker
                  (/encounter/oscarMeasurements/ViewHealthTracker?template=tracker).

  Deliberately ships with NO <header>/<item> elements. The Health Tracker is a
  per-provider/per-patient scratch flowsheet: clinicians populate it themselves
  through Edit Flowsheet, and those additions are stored as FlowSheetCustomization
  rows rather than in this file. The empty definition is what makes the page's
  "It looks like you are not tracking any measurements!" first-run state reachable.

  It also carries no is_universal / dxcode_triggers / program_triggers attributes.
  That is intentional: it keeps "tracker" out of getUniveralFlowsheets() and the
  dx-trigger tables, so the Health Tracker never renders as just another entry in
  the encounter left-nav flowsheet list. Its single nav entry is contributed by
  EctDisplayMeasurements2Action, gated on the health_tracker property.
-->
<flowsheet name="tracker" display_name="Health Tracker" ds_rules="tracker.drl" top_HTML="" warning_colour="#E00000" recommendation_colour="yellow">
    <indicator key="LOW" colour="#9999FF" />
    <indicator key="HIGH" colour="orange" />
    <indicator key="HIGH 1" colour="#E00000" />
</flowsheet>
